In Madi Satyavati v. State of Telangana 13, the Division Bench of this Court dealt with a matter pertaining to land acquisition for a railway project; and held that not only the mother, but also her three daughters, qualify as an affected family under Right to Fair Compensation and Transparency in Land Acquisition, Rehabilitation and Resettlement Act, 2013;
and modified a prior order to ensure that rehabilitation benefits are determined for the daughters in addition to the mother's solatium and allowed the appellants to seek a formal reference if they are dissatisfied with the final monetary compensation, reinforcing that the rights of all affected family members must be recognized in land acquisition cases.
